## Prices and supply by disposition

In absolute price, which is what a mortgage is granted against, the market looks different from the price per metre. A one-room flat costs {r1Price} € on average at {r1AreaEn} m², a two-room one {r2Price} € at {r2AreaEn} m², a three-room one {r3Price} € at {r3AreaEn} m², and a four-room or larger {r4Price} € at {r4AreaEn} m². The composition of supply leans to the middle: two-room flats are {r2ShareEn}% and three-room {r3ShareEn}%, against {r1ShareEn}% one-room and {r4ShareEn}% four-room or larger.

